# Cell from playpick: mode=clear, spec=paladin:retribution, style=wander,
# size=25, difficulty=heroic, view=844x390,touch, save=fresh. 25-heroic is
# locked at the door on a fresh save (src/progress.ts's RUNGS chain: a fresh
# save's `unlocked` is 0, and 25-heroic on the first boss sits at chain index
# 3) -- substituted the setup screen's own default, 10-player normal, the
# same substitution the three prior attempts at this cell made.
#
# Fourth attempt at this exact cell. The first three (plans -1, -2, -3;
# commits 2641416, e4be536, dc57b86) all ran `evening` and none left a ledger
# line -- two were started in the background and abandoned mid-run, the third
# split the walk into two chunks against a shared --profile/--out but still
# did not finish inside one turn. This session runs each chunk of the split
# to completion in the foreground before doing anything else, and writes the
# ledger line no matter how far the evening actually gets.
#
# Chunk 1: walk in, and as many rooms as fit in one blocking call. `--profile`
# and `--out` are passed on the command line and are shared with the chunks
# that follow, so `open` + `tap raid` below resumes exactly where this one
# stops (README: "RAID resumes standing where you stood").
open
targets
shot front
tap raid
shot raid-setup
tap next
tap class:paladin:retribution
shot class-selected
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
shot arrive-threshold
state
targets
evening wander 150 5
shot after-evening-1
state
says
